proposed_comments.body:
### MIME boundaries must match delimiter lines

**Severity:** `medium`

In a valid multipart email, `prefix --b suffix` is ordinary body text when `b` is the declared boundary. This splitter cuts at every `--b` substring, truncating the text and parsing the suffix as a malformed child, which causes the `.eml` preview to fail. Match complete delimiter lines with a valid suffix and return the intervening original bytes.

```suggestion
            string delimiter = $@"(?m)^--{Regex.Escape(boundary)}(?<closing>--)?[ \t]*(?:\r?\n|$)";
            int start = -1;
            foreach (Match match in Regex.Matches(body, delimiter, RegexOptions.None, TimeSpan.FromSeconds(1)))
            {
                if (start >= 0)
                {
                    int end = match.Index;
                    if (end > start && data[end - 1] == '\n')
                    {
                        end--;
                        if (end > start && data[end - 1] == '\r')
                        {
                            end--;
                        }
                    }

                    if (end > start)
                    {
                        yield return data[start..end];
                    }
                }

                if (match.Groups["closing"].Success)
                {
                    yield break;
                }

                start = match.Index + match.Length;
            }

            if (start >= 0 && start < data.Length)
            {
                yield return data[start..];
```

